---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url, REPO } from '../lib/catalog';
const GA4 = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_GA4_ID;
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What this site measures, what it does not, and how to refuse.">
  <section class="wrap-narrow section prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Short version: no account, no advertising, no profile. One thing is measured — how many
      people read which page — and only after you agree to it.
    </p>

    <h2>What is measured</h2>
    {GA4 ? (
      <>
        <p>
          Page views, through <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> (measurement ID
          <span class="mono"> {GA4}</span>, visible in the page source like everything else here).
          It answers one question we cannot answer otherwise: which parts of the catalogue are
          actually used, and therefore where the next work should go.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>The page you are on, when, and the page that sent you here.</li>
          <li>Approximate country and city, derived from a truncated IP address.</li>
          <li>Device type, browser and language.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Nothing is measured before you accept. Google Consent Mode starts with every category
          set to <span class="mono">denied</span>, so no measurement cookie is written until you
          click Accept — and if you click Refuse, none ever is.
        </p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <p>
        Nothing. No analytics is configured on this deployment: the site is static files served
        from GitHub Pages, and the page source contains no measurement script at all.
      </p>
    )}

    <h2>What is never done</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No advertising.</strong> The advertising categories of Consent Mode are hard-coded to <span class="mono">denied</span> and are never asked about.</li>
      <li><strong>No account, no login, no form.</strong> There is nothing to sign up for.</li>
      <li><strong>No third-party embeds.</strong> No social widgets, no comment system, no chat.</li>
      <li><strong>No data sold, shared or enriched.</strong> There is no CRM behind this site.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Vendor logos are served from this domain, not hot-linked from vendors' sites — so browsing
      the catalogue does not tell any of them that you looked.
    </p>

    <h2>Changing your mind</h2>
    <p>
      Your choice is stored in your browser's local storage under the key
      <span class="mono">pa-consent</span>, on this domain only. Clearing your site data resets
      it and the banner comes back. Browser-level Do Not Track and privacy modes are respected by
      the same mechanism, since a blocked script measures nothing.
    </p>

    <h2>A note for French readers</h2>
    <div class="callout">
      The CNIL grants a consent exemption to strictly necessary audience measurement, but Google
      Analytics does not qualify for it. That is precisely why this site asks rather than assumes,
      and why the default is <span class="mono">denied</span>. A cookieless alternative such as
      Plausible or a self-hosted Matomo configured to CNIL's exemption criteria would remove the
      banner entirely — it is <a href={`${REPO}/issues`} rel="noopener">an open question</a> on
      this project, not a settled one.
    </div>

    <h2>The data in the catalogue</h2>
    <p>
      Entries describe software products and the companies that publish them — business
      information, not personal data. Where a person is named, it is in a public professional
      capacity. If you are named here and would rather not be,
      <a href={`${REPO}/issues/new/choose`} rel="noopener">open an issue</a> and it will be
      removed.
    </p>

    <h2>Where this page lives</h2>
    <p>
      In the same public repository as everything else:
      <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/src/pages/privacy.astro`} rel="noopener">
        <span class="mono">src/pages/privacy.astro</span></a>. If it disagrees with what the site
      actually does, that is a bug — the measurement code is in
      <span class="mono">src/components/Analytics.astro</span> and it is twenty lines long.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
